              "qualification": "Uniform photosphere colour from the star's ground-based spectrophotometry (Pulkovo catalogue). The surface is darkened by latitude from the published Roche-von Zeipel fit of Zhao et al. (2009): the hot poles brighter and bluer, the cool equator dimmer and redder. The disc is unresolved: it is darkened toward the limb by the quadratic V-band law Claret & Bloemen (2011) compute from ATLAS model atmospheres at the star's temperature and gravity, a model rather than a measurement; no map or absolute brightness is implied. Self-luminous, so no lighting.",
